WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:18.546
Ten days passed, and there was no news of Mr.

2
00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:20.747
Rochester. Mrs.

3
00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:24.550
Fairfax said she wouldn't be surprised if he went abroad for a year.

4
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.273
He'd often left Thornfield in the past in an abrupt manner.

5
00:00:30.373 --> 00:00:33.856
When I heard this, I actually allowed myself to feel disappointed.

6
00:00:35.008 --> 00:00:40.271
But then I remembered that I had nothing to do with the master of Thornfield except to receive

7
00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:42.153
his salary for teaching Adele.

8
00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.035
I should not waste my love on someone who was above me.

9
00:00:47.236 --> 00:00:50.778
Mr. Rochester had been absent for more than two weeks when Mrs.

10
00:00:50.818 --> 00:00:52.179
Fairfax received a letter.

11
00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:58.763
"Now I suppose we'll know whether we're to expect his return or not," she said as she opened

12
00:00:58.823 --> 00:00:59.904
his letter at breakfast.

13
00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:05.011
My hand shook, and I spilled half my coffee as she read the letter.

14
00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:12.735
I tied Adele's pinafore, which happened to be loose, and then helped her to another bun and refilled

15
00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:15.357
her milk before I trusted myself to speak.

16
00:01:15.377 --> 00:01:19.039
"Mr. Rochester isn't likely to return soon?"

17
00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:21.340
I asked in a nonchalant voice.

18
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:28.028
"Indeed he's returning in three days and he's bringing some houseguests.

19
00:01:28.048 --> 00:01:32.390
He has given me instructions to hire some help from Millcote to prepare the house."

20
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.191
The next few days were busy.

21
00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:43.274
Mrs. Fairfax needed me in the kitchen, so I spent all my time helping—or hindering—the cook as she

22
00:01:43.314 --> 00:01:45.135
made pastries and prepared game.

23
00:01:46.316 --> 00:01:51.978
Since I was busy, Adele was excused from school and she ran wild with excitement.

24
00:01:53.038 --> 00:01:56.860
During these days the one blot on my happiness was Grace Poole.

25
00:01:57.932 --> 00:02:01.434
The dinner hour was the only time she spent with her fellow servants.

26
00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:05.736
But none of them seemed to think this was strange.

27
00:02:06.997 --> 00:02:13.781
One day I overheard one of the new servants from Millcote talking to Leah about Grace, but as

28
00:02:13.861 --> 00:02:16.202
soon as Leah spotted me, they stopped.

29
00:02:16.222 --> 00:02:18.143
"Doesn't she know?"

30
00:02:18.663 --> 00:02:19.544
whispered the woman.

31
00:02:20.744 --> 00:02:26.267
Leah shook her head, and I was reminded that there was a mystery at Thornfield and that I

32
00:02:26.327 --> 00:02:27.548
was excluded from it.

33
00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:33.571
At last that evening we heard the clatter of hoofbeats that signaled the arrival of Mr.

34
00:02:33.631 --> 00:02:35.192
Rochester and his party.

35
00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:38.653
Looking out a window, I saw Mr.

36
00:02:38.753 --> 00:02:46.498
Rochester and a dark-haired woman, who had to be Blanche Ingram, galloping on horseback ahead of two carriages

37
00:02:46.638 --> 00:02:48.179
full of ladies and gentlemen.

38
00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:56.043
After the ladies had changed, Adele longed to go downstairs and see their beautiful dresses, but we had

39
00:02:56.123 --> 00:02:58.184
our supper upstairs in the schoolroom.

40
00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.682
I told her stories for as long as she would listen.

41
00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:08.407
Then we sat on the stairs as the sound of a piano floated up from the sitting room.

42
00:03:09.548 --> 00:03:12.250
A woman sang, and then we heard a duet.

43
00:03:13.471 --> 00:03:14.512
I listened for Mr.

44
00:03:14.592 --> 00:03:15.673
Rochester's voice.

45
00:03:16.854 --> 00:03:18.315
The next day Mrs.

46
00:03:18.355 --> 00:03:20.377
Fairfax said she'd mentioned to Mr.

47
00:03:20.457 --> 00:03:24.260
Rochester that Adele wanted to be introduced to the ladies.

48
00:03:25.421 --> 00:03:29.044
He'd said that Adele and I should come to the sitting room after dinner.

49
00:03:30.348 --> 00:03:37.375
And so, wearing my best gray dress, the one I'd worn only to Miss Temple's wedding, I settled

50
00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:39.917
myself unobtrusively on a window seat.

51
00:03:41.138 --> 00:03:43.561
Suddenly six ladies entered the room.

52
00:03:44.662 --> 00:03:52.049
Mrs. Eshton had two pretty daughters, Amy and Louisa, but they could not compete with Lady Ingram and

53
00:03:52.089 --> 00:03:55.412
her tall, beautiful daughters, Mary and Blanche.

54
00:03:56.612 --> 00:04:02.134
No longer able to contain her excitement, Adele ran over and greeted them in French.

55
00:04:04.174 --> 00:04:10.116
Blanche looked down at her with disdain, but the Eshton girls exclaimed with delight over Adele.

56
00:04:11.256 --> 00:04:15.357
They led her to a sofa, where she chattered away in French and English.

57
00:04:16.678 --> 00:04:20.859
At last coffee was served, and the gentlemen entered the room: Mr.

58
00:04:20.939 --> 00:04:22.239
Rochester, Mr.

59
00:04:22.359 --> 00:04:26.293
Eshton, and Theodore Ingram, brother of Mary and Blanche.

60
00:04:27.453 --> 00:04:31.954
Mr. Rochester didn't even glance my way, so I was free to watch him.

61
00:04:33.275 --> 00:04:36.656
Reader, you know I did not intend to love him.

62
00:04:37.836 --> 00:04:41.837
In fact, I had worked hard at pulling the roots of love from my soul.

63
00:04:42.917 --> 00:04:45.658
But he made me love him without looking at me.

64
00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:51.180
I knew I must conceal my feelings and remember that he couldn't care for me.

65
00:04:52.444 --> 00:04:55.766
Mr. Rochester had not noticed me, but Blanche had.

66
00:04:55.786 --> 00:04:58.948
"Why didn't you send Adele to school?"

67
00:04:59.348 --> 00:05:00.048
she asked Mr.

68
00:05:00.088 --> 00:05:05.351
Rochester. "A governess is such a nuisance."

69
00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.392
"I couldn't afford it," replied Mr.

70
00:05:07.452 --> 00:05:09.654
Rochester, still not looking at me.

71
00:05:09.674 --> 00:05:12.155
"Schools are expensive."

72
00:05:12.175 --> 00:05:17.338
"Theodore and I used to delight in tormenting our governesses with tricks.

73
00:05:18.579 --> 00:05:20.860
Do you remember those merry days, Theodore?"

74
00:05:21.956 --> 00:05:24.917
"Indeed I do," replied her brother with a laugh.

75
00:05:26.057 --> 00:05:29.358
Blanche now seated herself with proud grace at the piano.

76
00:05:30.459 --> 00:05:36.000
Spreading out her dress like a queen, she played a brilliant prelude, talking all the time.

77
00:05:37.201 --> 00:05:43.222
Both her words and her manner seemed intended to excite the admiration and amazement of her listeners.

78
00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.563
"Oh, I'm sick of today's young men!"

79
00:05:47.084 --> 00:05:47.884
she exclaimed.

80
00:05:48.992 --> 00:05:54.434
"They can't do anything without their mama's permission, and they're so absorbed in their own pretty faces.

81
00:05:55.575 --> 00:06:00.496
When I marry, I'll refuse to share my husband with the image he sees in his mirror."

82
00:06:02.317 --> 00:06:04.438
She paused, but no one said anything.

83
00:06:04.458 --> 00:06:06.659
"Now sing, Mr.

84
00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.960
Rochester," she commanded, "and I will play for you."

85
00:06:11.192 --> 00:06:17.095
"I am all obedience" was his response, and he began to sing in a powerful bass voice that

86
00:06:17.235 --> 00:06:19.217
quickly found its way into my heart.

87
00:06:20.377 --> 00:06:24.619
Now was my time to slip away, but I found I could not leave until Mr.

88
00:06:24.679 --> 00:06:25.720
Rochester finished.

89
00:06:26.841 --> 00:06:30.683
When the song ended and conversation began, I left the room.

90
00:06:31.763 --> 00:06:36.146
Crossing the hall, I noticed that my shoe was loose, so I bent to tie it.

91
00:06:37.386 --> 00:06:40.008
I heard a door open and a man come into the hall.

92
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.241
Rising hastily, I came face to face with Mr.

93
00:06:44.301 --> 00:06:46.622
Rochester. "How do you do?"

94
00:06:46.942 --> 00:06:47.442
he asked.

95
00:06:47.462 --> 00:06:49.442
"I'm very well, sir."

96
00:06:49.462 --> 00:06:52.283
"Why didn't you come over and speak to me?"

97
00:06:52.303 --> 00:06:56.664
"I didn't want to disturb you as you seemed engaged, sir."

98
00:06:56.684 --> 00:07:00.285
"What have you been doing during my absence?"

99
00:07:01.626 --> 00:07:03.286
"Only teaching Adele as usual."

100
00:07:03.306 --> 00:07:06.467
"And getting a good deal paler than you were.

101
00:07:07.547 --> 00:07:08.127
What's the matter?"

102
00:07:08.147 --> 00:07:09.908
"Nothing at all, sir.

103
00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:11.588
I'm just tired."

104
00:07:11.608 --> 00:07:14.550
"And a little depressed too," he said.

105
00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:16.371
"Tell me what's wrong."

106
00:07:17.491 --> 00:07:19.152
"Nothing nothing, sir.

107
00:07:20.252 --> 00:07:21.033
I'm not depressed."

108
00:07:21.053 --> 00:07:23.374
"But you are depressed.

109
00:07:24.554 --> 00:07:26.335
A few more words and you would be crying.

110
00:07:27.376 --> 00:07:29.316
There, I see a tear in your eye even now."

111
00:07:30.477 --> 00:07:32.898
He looked at me with some concern and tenderness.

112
00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:39.587
"Well, I'll excuse you for leaving early tonight, but as long as my visitors stay, I expect you

113
00:07:39.607 --> 00:07:41.669
to appear in the sitting room every evening.

114
00:07:42.811 --> 00:07:48.157
Now goodnight, my He stopped, bit his lip, and abruptly left me.
